my name is a concussion and I'm a senior  in electrical engineering and computer  science so my the goal of my project was  to use capnography to diagnose between  two cardio respiratory conditions  congestive heart failure and chronic  obstructive pulmonary disease so the  problem is that there's a lot of people  suffering from respiratory conditions  however the diagnostic tests that are  used to diagnose these conditions  require a lot of effort from the patient  and they might be very hard to comply  with if the patient is under a lot of  distress so what we want to do is  replace these tests with capnography  which is effort independent and very  easy to comply with so capnography  measures the partial pressure of carbon  dioxide in exhaled breath as the patient  is breathing normally and produces a  graph called a capnogram and these  capnogram have distinct shapes for  different cardio respiratory conditions  so the first step is to produce a  mechanistic model that is based on the  compartmental models of the respiratory  system that produces an expression for  the partial pressure of carbon dioxide  or the capnogram as a function of  respiratory parameters and these  respiratory parameters are  physiologically relevant so the first  step is to pre-process our capnogram to  extract the portions of the capnogram  corresponding to exhalation and then fit  our mechanistic model to these  accelerations to extract these  respiratory parameters and use these  respiratory parameters to actually  diagnose between the two conditions  so using these estimated parameters in a  training set we train a quadratic  discriminator and we use this quadratic  discriminator on a test set and applied  it on a patient by patient basis to  obtain an accuracy of around eighty  seven point five percent which was very  successful
 

